.TH OPTCHAT 1 "" "OptChat @VERSION@" "User Commands"
.SH NAME
optchat \- native OptChat engine client
.SH SYNOPSIS
.B optchat
.SH DESCRIPTION
OptChat connects to an OptChat engine and displays its workspaces, chats and tasks.
Open Workspaces, choose Add engine, and enter a scoped client token to connect.
The application also provides file attachments and dictation.
.PP
OptChat can be started from a terminal or the desktop application menu.
Press Ctrl+K to open the command palette, F11 to toggle full screen,
and Ctrl+Q to quit.
.SH ENVIRONMENT
.TP
.B XDG_CONFIG_HOME
The base directory for application preferences.
OptChat uses the optchat subdirectory and defaults to ~/.config/optchat.
.SH FILES
.TP
.B ~/.config/optchat
Application preferences. Removing the package preserves this directory.
.PP
Engine tokens are stored in the desktop Secret Service keyring.
.SH SEE ALSO
Project documentation: https://github.com/fabihatasneem/optchat-client
